Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:02:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Runner: the waiting screen's counts, tags and "YOU" in the
 names' font

Gibax: "pour cet ecran met la police qu'on a fait", and "pouvoir aussi
ajouter le tag d'un joueur". The waiting screen's "8 PLAYERS", "8 RACERS",
"2/8 READY" and "YOU", and each seat's tag (SRNP_TAGS, under its card),
are written in the font of the results' names.

- srnp_labels: NameFontText() lays any text out in that font (the
  names' letters, the others from Saira, now with '/'), and PlayerTag()
  gives a seat's tag.
- srnp_game_textures: NameText() reads "GoalResult_01_E" from the
  player's GTSE file (the 7th GVR texture; the game has loaded nothing
  yet while it waits), lays the text out and makes it an ImGui texture,
  cached per text.
- srnp_waiting_screen: the counts as one line with a gap between them,
  made smaller together when needed; every tag the size at which 8 wide
  letters fit a column; "YOU" in the menus' yellow under the tag. Without
  the GTSE, the ImGui text as before.

Seen on two runners waiting for 8 seats (2/8), tags GIBAX, TAILSMKR,
K-NUX, AMY_R, -, WAVE!, BOB-PIP, ZAP-2024.

